    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ✂️ Split & Rename\nSplits a multi-file upload into **one item per PDF** and renames each binary to `data` (the name the Extractor expects). Also **resets the flag buffer** so warnings from a previous run don't carry over.",
        "height": 336,
        "width": 256,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [-272, 208],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "43984c6a-ee4e-4b87-b6ee-5eb555c18dca",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔁 One PO at a time\nBatch size **1**. The Extractor bundles all inputs into a single call, so each PDF must pass through on its own. The **loop** output processes each PO, the **done** output fires once at the end.",
        "height": 336,
        "width": 256,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [0, 208],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "12d9914e-0345-4d6a-8dc0-cf2ac38301c5",
      "name": "Sticky Note2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🚩 Build Warnings\nReads the flags collected during the run and builds the message for the end screen. If nothing was flagged, it reports a **clean extraction**. Runs once, on the loop's **done** output.",
        "height": 352,
        "width": 256,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [272, 32],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "1d8ea34f-6d87-4626-98c1-349f35e2b473",
      "name": "Sticky Note3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🤖 Extract with easybits\nReads the header fields and the full article table from one PDF. Output is wrapped in a `data` envelope. Field setup lives in the Extractor credential – see the main note for the field list and descriptions.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 256,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [272, 400],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "619f220b-7416-4650-b6fb-9eb504a1b520",
      "name": "Sticky Note4"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🧩 Flatten to Rows\nTurns each PO into **one row per article**, stapling the header fields (PO Number, dates, Mark For, PR Number) onto every line. Adds the **Document Name**. Cleans every empty value (`null`, `NULL`, `\"\"`, blanks) to an empty cell and **records a flag** per document if anything is missing.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 256,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [544, 400],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "5320af28-70a2-4af5-8f55-1766402fb426",
      "name": "Sticky Note5"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📊 Write to Sheet\nAppends every article row to the Google Sheet. **RAW** value mode keeps quantities and special characters literal. Columns map automatically – the header row in the sheet must match the field names exactly.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 256,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [1856, 432],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "0d0393fe-5816-4f71-9fd8-47de9b37e5b0",
      "name": "Sticky Note6"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ✅ End Screen\nShows the user the result after processing. Lists **which documents and which fields** may not have extracted fully, so they know what to double-check against the original PDF.",
        "height": 352,
        "width": 256,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [544, 32],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "7b5b6eef-0914-4d65-8cab-085baa83f7d9",
      "name": "Sticky Note7"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🛡️ Guardian Check\nEvaluates the PO against Guardian policy before writing to the sheet.\n\n**3 outputs:**\n- **Allowed** → rows go to the sheet\n- **Denied** → rows skipped, loop continues\n- **Needs Approval** → rows skipped, approver gets notified in Guardian\n\nIn **Listen Mode**, everything goes through Allowed (OBSERVED). Check the audit trail to see what *would* have been denied, then create policies and turn off Listen Mode.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [816, 432],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "note-guardian-check",
      "name": "Sticky Note8"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔄 Async Approval Flow\nWhen a PO needs approval, the workflow doesn't wait. Once the approver clicks **Approve** (or **Edit & Approve**) in the Guardian dashboard:\n\n1. **Guardian Approval Trigger** fires\n2. **Guardian Execute** confirms the intent (atomically claims it — no duplicates)\n3. Rows are split out and written to the sheet\n\nNo manual webhook setup — the trigger auto-registers when the workflow is activated.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [816, 800],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "note-approval-flow",
      "name": "Sticky Note9"
    },
